      "turn": 12,
      "speaker": "Y",
      "kind": "message",
      "segment": "conversation",
      "text": "Gödel's theorems are fascinating. They reveal the inherent limitations of formal systems capable of expressing arithmetic. It’s striking that no matter how comprehensive we make our axiomatic system, there will always be truths it can’t prove.",
