      "id": "line-15",
      "parent": null,
      "turn": 14,
      "speaker": "Y",
      "kind": "message",
      "segment": "conversation",
      "text": "They have profound implications for both. In computing, for example, we can’t have an algorithm that can determine the truth or falsehood of every statement in a sufficiently expressive system. For AI, it suggests there will always be limits to what can be computed or proven automatically, no matter how advanced the system becomes.",
